From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:13:12 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 62/95] Plutonium: an input method composes and commits into
 embedded windows

EXO-EMBED stopped the propagation of every key for an embedded window, so
the page whose view a key was aimed at didn't also get it. That included
the input method's own keys: the VKEY_PROCESSKEY it sends before
composing or committing, and the key it passes on before committing a
single character. InputMethodAsh reads a stopped key as taken by its
target and drops the composition or the commit, so an IME's text never
reached a native window. Those keys are now only marked handled, which
keeps them from the page all the same.

Verified with an extension IME (chrome.input.ime) and gtk4-demo over
zwp_text_input_v3 on Xvfb.
---
 components/exo/keyboard.cc | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/exo/keyboard.cc b/components/exo/keyboard.cc
index fcee60ef4f..681559132d 100644
--- a/components/exo/keyboard.cc
+++ b/components/exo/keyboard.cc
@@ -283,7 +283,15 @@ void Keyboard::ProcessKeyEvent(ui::KeyEvent* event) {
   // the page whose view they were aimed at.
   absl::Cleanup stop_embedded_propagation = [this, event] {
     if (embedded_owner_) {
-      event->StopPropagation();
+      // A key the input method handled (its VKEY_PROCESSKEY, or the key it
+      // passes on before committing a character) is only marked handled:
+      // InputMethodAsh drops the composition or commit when that key's
+      // propagation is stopped.
+      if (ConsumedByIme(*event)) {
+        event->SetHandled();
+      } else {
+        event->StopPropagation();
+      }
     }
   };
 
